*** Settings ***
Documentation       Unmodified STM32CubeU5 HAL (v1.9.0 components) on USART1 at 115200 baud from
...                 PCLK2 = 160 MHz (firmware-tests/stm32cube/uart): HAL_UART_Init with FIFO
...                 configuration as generated by STM32CubeMX, transmit by polling and by interrupt,
...                 receive by interrupt with an upper-case echo.
Resource            ${CURDIR}/../common/stm32u575.resource
Test Setup          Run HAL UART Firmware

*** Variables ***
${ELF}              ${ROOT}/build/firmware/hal-uart.elf
${UART}             sysbus.usart1
${STEP_RECEIVING}   12
${UNMODELLED_ACCESS}    Unhandled (read|write)|non existing peripheral

*** Keywords ***
Run HAL UART Firmware
    Create STM32U575 Machine
    Create Log Tester               0
    Execute Command                 $bin=@${ELF}
    Execute Command                 macro reset "sysbus LoadELF $bin"
    Execute Command                 runMacro $reset
    Create Terminal Tester          ${UART}    defaultPauseEmulation=true

Read Symbol
    [Arguments]                     ${symbol}
    ${address}=                     Execute Command    sysbus GetSymbolAddress "${symbol}"
    ${address}=                     Strip String       ${address}
    ${value}=                       Read Word          ${address}
    RETURN                          ${value}

Receiving Should Have Started
    ${step}=                        Read Symbol        step
    Should Be Equal As Integers     ${step}            ${STEP_RECEIVING}

*** Test Cases ***
Should Print Using Polling And Interrupt Transmission
    Wait For Line On Uart           STM32U575 HAL UART ready
    Wait For Line On Uart           Interrupt transmit done
    ${failed}=                      Read Symbol        failedStep
    Should Be Equal As Integers     ${failed}          0

Should Configure 115200 Baud From The 160 MHz Kernel Clock
    Wait For Line On Uart           Interrupt transmit done
    # BRR = round(160 MHz / 115200) = 1389 (RM0456 section 66.5.8, oversampling by 16).
    ${brr}=                         Read Symbol        usartBrr
    Should Be Equal As Integers     ${brr}             1389
    Property Should Be              usart1 Frequency   160000000
    Property Should Be              usart1 BaudRate    115190

Should Echo Received Characters In Upper Case
    Wait For Line On Uart           Interrupt transmit done
    # The terminal tester pauses the emulation on a match; let the firmware start reception.
    Execute Command                 emulation RunFor "0.01"
    Receiving Should Have Started
    Write To Uart                   hello renode
    Wait For Prompt On Uart         HELLO RENODE
    ${count}=                       Read Symbol        receivedCount
    Should Be Equal As Integers     ${count}           12

Should Not Touch Unmodelled Registers
    Wait For Line On Uart           Interrupt transmit done
    Execute Command                 emulation RunFor "0.01"
    Write To Uart                   x
    Wait For Prompt On Uart         X
    Should Not Be In Log            ${UNMODELLED_ACCESS}    treatAsRegex=true
